! mcp_bootstrap_p144.strap -- "RETURN AFTER MASKABLE INTERRUPT",
! printed page 144.  docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.151, header
! read and not assumed: the top line prints "TIME CLOCK 00054041
! PUNID 11011MCP   CARD ID FB000001   DIST. OF 3/01   3/01
! PAGE NUMBER 144".
!
! WHAT THE PAGE IS.  Thirty printed lines.  Lines 1-4 are the
! asterisk box around the heading "*****RETURN AFTER MASKABLE
! INTERRUPT *****" (line 2); line 5 is "SLC,$"; lines 6-30 are
! twenty-five instructions, every one of them CODE.  No SYN, no
! DD, no VF, no DRZ, no data of any kind.  The routine is the one
! C22-6728-1 (MCP System Analysis Guide) names in prose: "control
! returned to the point of interrupt via the return after maskable
! interrupt routine", reached from the Program Table of Exits.
!
! The body is three exits that share one tail:
!   WRAMPP (line 6)  the PP entry.  SR,15,$1 lifts the PTOE address
!                    out of X15's refill field, the two KV/branch
!                    pairs bounds-check it against S LOWER / S UPPER
!                    and go to W JERR if it is outside PP storage,
!                    CM0000 takes the PP out of special fixup, the
!                    TI restores $LZC, and BBZ,STSBIT goes to
!                    JWRAM1 if a TS was stacked.
!   W CON 1 (line 14) the common restore: LV picks up the interrupt
!                    address, BB tests bit 18 (the EXE bit) and goes
!                    to JWFINI if the PP tries to restore EXE, SVA
!                    plants the address in W FINI, two TIs restore
!                    the indicators+mask and the used index
!                    registers, and line 19's "W FINI BE,$" is the
!                    modified branch that returns.
!   JWFINI (line 20) and JWRAM1 (line 26) are the two fake-exit
!                    tails: each plants the address in S TIC instead
!                    and branches into the parallel interrupt table,
!                    S IPT+18.0 to fake EXE (line 23) and S IPT+4.0
!                    to fake TS (line 30).
!   WRAM   (line 24) the MCP entry -- LVI,1,SFPTE loads the MCP PTOE
!                    and falls into W CON 1.
!
! TWENTY-EIGHT CARDS OVER THIRTY LINES.  The serial column runs
! FB000001 (line 1) to FB000028 (line 30) with FB000007 printed on
! lines 7 AND 8 and FB000008 on lines 9 AND 10 -- two cards that
! each carry two statements, exactly as printed p.130's EC000015
! and EC000016 do for the SAME two pairs.  Nothing is missing off
! the top or the bottom of the render.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE JOIN, CLOSED FROM BOTH SIDES
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LINE 5 PRINTS "217326.00 *  SLC,$" AND THAT IS A FREE WITNESS.
! An SLC emits nothing, so its printed LOCATION *is* the counter
! arriving from the previous page.  This deck writes a hard
! "SLC,(8)217326.0" so it assembles standalone, which ASSERTS the
! origin rather than checking it (docs/transcription_workflow.md,
! "A HARD SLC CANNOT DISAGREE WITH THE ARRIVING COUNTER"), so the
! printed value is recorded here and in the !CHECK note instead.
!
! NEAR SIDE: printed p.143 (PDF p.150) ends at line 27, a half-word
!   branch "B,JTSEX3" whose printed LOCATION is 217325.40, so the
!   counter leaves p.143 at exactly 217326.00.  (Read out of the
!   volume OCR, which is a legitimate index onto ANOTHER page.)
!   p.143's line 26, at 217325.00, is "LVI,$1,S IPT+18.0" printing
!   215125.03 -- the same S IPT base lines 23 and 30 here use.
! FAR SIDE: the volume OCR carries, on a page near 220764,
!   "220764.40  217326.10 00  B,WRAMPP  -RETURN AFTER MASKABLE".
!   A plain B prints target+.10, so WRAMPP is at 217326.00 -- this
!   page's first label, read off a different page.
! Both agree with line 6's printed 217326.00.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! GLYPHS -- WHAT WAS SETTLED AND ON WHAT
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! This page opens round glyphs constantly: its own column heading
! prints "LCCATICN", and locations print "217326.CC" for .00.
! Every round glyph in a LOCATION or in an octal BINARY field is a
! 0 with certainty (C is not an octal digit).  The glyphs that are
! NOT in an octal field were each settled on something else.
!
! (1) >>> THE PAGE CALIBRATES ITSELF, TWICE, AND THIS IS THE
!     STRONGEST EVIDENCE HERE. <<<  Lines 14 and 26 are the SAME
!     STATEMENT and compile to the same word, and the drum prints
!     them differently:
!         line 14   W CON 1   LV,0,0.0($1)      000000.00 31
!         line 26   JWRAM1    LV,C,C.C($1)      000000.00 31
!     Same instruction, same bits, one printed with closed zeros
!     and one with open C's, on one page off one drum.  Lines 17
!     and 28 do it again ("TI,2,1.0($1),$IND" vs "TI,2,1.C($1),
!     $INC").  So an open round glyph in a STATEMENT on this page
!     is an ordinary 0, with no OCR and no other page involved.
!
! (2) "$C" IS "$0", AND THE ASSEMBLER ELIMINATES THE OTHER READING.
!     Lines 18, 22 and 29 print "TI,4,STLR+13.0,$C".  Measured:
!         TI,4,STLR+13.0,$0     215245.00 80  000020.10 A0  = PRINTED
!         TI,4,STLR+13.0,$C     "unsupported system symbol $'C'"
!     There is no register $C; $0 is index register 0 at word 0o20,
!     and its 19-bit A2 plus J=4 is exactly the printed .10.  The
!     operand is therefore ORACLE-CHECKED, not read off ink.
!
! (3) "$INC" IS "$IND", by the comment column and by the bits.
!     Line 17's comment is "-RESTORE IND + MASK REGS." -- the word
!     is IND -- and $IND is word 11, whose A2 prints 000013.04 with
!     J=2, which is what the page prints.
!
! (4) "$LZC" vs "$AOC", settled on the bits.  Both live in word 7
!     ($LZC bits 17-23, $AOC bits 44-50), so the glyph does not
!     have to decide it.  Measured:
!         TI,1,STLR+4.0,$LZC    000007.02 A0   = PRINTED
!         TI,1,STLR+4.0,$AOC    000007.42 A0
!     Printed is .02, so it is $LZC.
!
! (5) "CMOCOO" IS "CM0000", AND IT IS CHECKED, NOT GUESSED.  The
!     connective's four digits land in the second half word's
!     offset field, so the oracle sees them.  Measured, with
!     everything else fixed:
!         CM0000(BU,1),SSPFIX   001000.00 F0   = PRINTED
!         CM0011(BU,1),SSPFIX   001000.06 F0
!         CM1100(BU,1),SSPFIX   001000.30 F0
!         CM1111(BU,1),SSPFIX   001000.36 F0
!     All four are distinct and only CM0000 matches.  printed p.130
!     line 19 independently prints "CM0000(BU,1),WCONY.21" against
!     the same "001000.00 F0", and p.130's line 13 prints the
!     CM1111 form against "001000.36 F0" -- the pair that this
!     measurement predicts.
!
! (6) THE TRAILING BYTE "FC" ON LINE 11 IS F0.  Hex field, so C is
!     legal there and the octal-field calibration does NOT settle
!     it.  It is settled on what produced it: the low nibble of a
!     VFL full word is i2, the offset index, and there is no second
!     operand, so it is 0.  printed p.18 prints "CM1111(BU,1)" six
!     times and every one is "001000.36 F0".  Likewise lines 12,
!     17, 18, 21, 22, 28, 29 print "AC" for A0 by the same rule.
!
! (7) THE "1" AT THE END OF "W CON 1" AND "JWRAM1" IS A DIGIT, NOT
!     AN I.  Nothing outside this page references either name, so
!     listing_oracle cannot see it and the name rests on ink; read
!     at 1800 dpi against this page's own I's one row away.  The
!     terminal glyph of both has the drum's digit-1 shape -- a
!     top-left flag stroke into a bare vertical stem with a base
!     serif and NO top bar -- and the I's of "JWFINI" and "W FINI"
!     directly below have full horizontal serifs top AND bottom.
!     The two shapes are not close at that magnification.
!     (This mattered: the volume carries a real WCONA at 216237.40
!     and a real WCON at 216343.40, so a neighbouring name family
!     exists and "obviously 1" was not safe.)
!
! (8) "WRAM" (line 24) ends in M, and printed p.133 lines 18-19
!     both print "B,WRAM" compiling 217343.10 -- this page's own
!     address, read by a different transcriber on a different page.
!     decks/mcp_bootstrap_p133.strap already SYNs WRAM at
!     217343.00.
!
! (9) "BXL"/"BZXL" and "BOPZ"-style mnemonics: the operation set is
!     small, and both of these assemble to exactly the printed
!     bytes (42 and 40), so the B/8 question does not arise.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! LABELS PRINTED WITH BLANKS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! "W CON 1" (line 14) and "W FINI" (line 19) print with blanks and
! are written closed up, WCON1 and WFINI, as every deck since p.2
! does -- the deck format takes a label to the first blank.  Both
! are six characters closed up, inside the six-character limit
! (C22-6531 printed p.10).  The page's own references print them
! ALREADY closed up ("B,WCON1" line 25, "SVA,0,WFINI" line 16),
! which is the assembler's own witness that the closed-up form is
! the name.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE TWO ASTERISKS, AND A READING THAT DIES ON THIS PAGE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Every one of the thirty line numbers carries an asterisk right
! after it ("6*", "30*").  That is the ordinary column.
!
! TWO lines carry a SECOND asterisk after the LOCATION: line 5
! (217326.00, the SLC) and LINE 21 (217340.40).  This is the
! unexplained marker of docs/listing_typography.md 12 and nothing
! here explains it.  What this page DISCONFIRMS: the tempting
! reading "a full word landing on an ODD half word is marked" --
! line 21 is a full-word TI at 217340.40 -- dies immediately,
! because lines 11 (217330.40), 17 (217335.40) and 22 (217341.40)
! are also full words on odd half words and carry NO mark.  Line
! 21 is also byte-for-byte identical to lines 17 and 28, which are
! unmarked.  Recorded as open, with nothing added to it.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS -- every one pinned by a card on a DIFFERENT page
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! ZERO TAUTOLOGICAL ROWS.  This page's own rows sit at OCR lines
! ~7569-7598 of docs/ocr/MCP_Mar63_001-249.txt; every witness cited
! below is at a different OCR line and a different printed page, so
! none of them is this page reading itself.  Seven of the nine are
! already carried by LANDED decks at these same values.
!
! S COM RG 215001.00  p.103 line 8 "S COM RG XW,(8)520000.".
!                     Carried only so S SPFIX and S TSBIT can be
!                     written the way p.103 writes them.
SCOMRG  SYN, (8)215001.0
! S SPFIX  215001.13  p.103 line 20 DEFINES it, "S SPFIX SYN(BU,1),
!                     S COM RG+.11" -ON IF PP IN SPECIAL FIXUP,
!                     printing the resolved 215001.13+.  Line 11
!                     here prints 215001.13 as a full 24-bit BIT
!                     address, so this row pins it to the BIT.
SSPFIX  SYN(BU,1), SCOMRG+.11
! S TSBIT  215001.14  p.103 line 21 DEFINES it, "S TSBIT SYN(BU,1),
!                     S COM RG+.12" -ON IF TS STACKED FOR PP.
!                     Line 13 here prints the bit address in full.
STSBIT  SYN(BU,1), SCOMRG+.12
! S T LR   215230.00  p.116 line 13 is the defining card, "S T LR
!                     DRZ(BU,64),29".  TI's A1 is a full 24-bit
!                     address, so lines 12/18 ("S TLR+4.0" ->
!                     215234.00, "S TLR+13.0" -> 215245.00) pin it
!                     to the bit from THIS page alone as well.
STLR    SYN, (8)215230.0
! S UPPER  215230.00  p.116 line 14 "S UPPER SYN,S T LR" -PP UPPER
!                     BOUNDRY.  It is the SAME ADDRESS as S T LR by
!                     construction -- that is not a collision.
SUPPER  SYN, STLR
! S LOWER  215230.40  p.116 line 15 "S LOWER SYN,S T LR+0.32"; 32
!                     decimal is bit 0o40.  KV only pins the half
!                     word, but the volume also prints
!                     "L(BU,18),SLOWER,46" against 215230.40 and
!                     "KV,$X1,S TLR+0.32 -COMPARE TO PP LOWER
!                     BOUNDRY" against 215230.42, so the bit is
!                     pinned too.
SLOWER  SYN, STLR+0.32
! S TIC    215265.00  p.116 line 16 "S T IC VF,0"; pp.110-112,
!                     117, 118 carry it.  SVA pins only the half
!                     word, but the volume prints "L(BU,1),
!                     STIC+.18,2" against 215265.22 -- a VFL bit
!                     address -- so S TIC is 215265.00 exactly.
!                     Final letter is C, not O: C22-6728 prose,
!                     "the saved IC is stored in STIC".
STIC    SYN, (8)215265.0
! S IPT    215103.00  p.112 line 7 DEFINES it, "S IPT BEW,$" at
!                     215103.00 -BASE ADDRESS OF PARALLEL
!                     INTERRUPT TABLE -- that card is the
!                     independent pin.  Lines 23 and 30 here check
!                     the arithmetic against two different printed
!                     words off the one base: "S IPT+18.0" ->
!                     215125.00 and "S IPT+4.0" -> 215107.00, and
!                     215125 - 0o22 = 215107 - 0o4 = 215103.
SIPT    SYN, (8)215103.0
! S FPTE   215163.00  p.114 line 5 "S FPTE DRZ(N),(3)" -- the MCP
!                     Program Table of Exits.  Independently, the
!                     volume prints "WPATT SYN,SFPTE+3.0" resolving
!                     to 215166.00, and 215166 - 3 = 215163.
SFPTE   SYN, (8)215163.0
! W JERR   216372.00  decks/mcp_bootstrap_p130.strap DEFINES it --
!                     p.130 line 51, "W JERR LVI,$14,SPTOEX" at
!                     216372.00 -- and p.130 lines 15-18 are the
!                     SAME FOUR STATEMENTS as lines 7-10 here, with
!                     the same four printed half words.  BXL/BZXL
!                     pin only the half word; p.130's label pins
!                     the rest.
WJERR   SYN, (8)216372.0

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE ORIGIN.  The page prints "SLC,$" (line 5, at 217326.00).
! Restated hard so the deck assembles standalone; see THE JOIN.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
        SLC, (8)217326.0

! ---- the routine -------------------------------------------------
WRAMPP  SR,15,$1                     ! line  6  -GET PTOE
        KV,$1,SLOWER                 ! line  7
        BXL,WJERR                    ! line  8  (same card as 7)
        KV,$1,SUPPER                 ! line  9
        BZXL,WJERR                   ! line 10  (same card as 9)
        CM0000(BU,1),SSPFIX          ! line 11  -TAKE PP OUT OF SPECIAL
        TI,1,STLR+4.0,$LZC           ! line 12
        BBZ,STSBIT,JWRAM1            ! line 13  -IF TS STACKED
WCON1   LV,0,0.0($1)                 ! line 14  -GET INT. AD.
        BB,1.18($1),JWFINI           ! line 15  -IF PP TRIES TO RESTORE EXE
        SVA,0,WFINI                  ! line 16  -SET TOE ADDRESS
        TI,2,1.0($1),$IND            ! line 17  -RESTORE IND + MASK REGS.
        TI,4,STLR+13.0,$0            ! line 18  -RESTORE USED INDEX REGS
WFINI   BE,$                         ! line 19  -RETURN TO PP INTERRUPTED ADDRESS
JWFINI  SVA,$0,STIC                  ! line 20  -MUST FAKE EXE
        TI,2,1.0($1),$IND            ! line 21
        TI,4,STLR+13.0,$0            ! line 22
        B,SIPT+18.0                  ! line 23  - FAKE EXE
WRAM    LVI,1,SFPTE                  ! line 24
        B,WCON1                      ! line 25
JWRAM1  LV,0,0.0($1)                 ! line 26
        SVA,0,STIC                   ! line 27
        TI,2,1.0($1),$IND            ! line 28
        TI,4,STLR+13.0,$0            ! line 29
        B,SIPT+4.0                   ! line 30  -FAKE TS

! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE PRINTED LISTING, AS RENDERED AT 400/900/1800 dpi
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   1*                                              - ****************************************************  FB000001
!   2*                                              -      *****RETURN AFTER MASKABLE INTERRUPT *****       FB000002
!   3*                                              - ****************************************************  FB000003
!   4*                                              -                                                       FB000004
!   5*  217326.00 *                                           SLC,$                                         FB000005
!   6*  217326.00   000021.37 70            WRAMPP   SR,15,$1                   -GET PTOE                   FB000006
!   7*  217326.40   215230.42 90                     KV,$1,SLOWER                                           FB000007
!   8*  217327.00   216372.32 42                     BXL,WJERR                                              FB000007
!   9*  217327.40   215230.02 90                     KV,$1,SUPPER                                           FB000008
!  10*  217330.00   216372.32 40                     BZXL,WJERR                                             FB000008
!  11*  217330.40   215001.13 80  001000.00 F0       CM0000(BU,1),SSPFIX        -TAKE PP OUT OF SPECIAL     FB000009
!  12*  217331.40   215234.00 80  000007.02 A0       TI,1,STLR+4.0,$LZC                                     FB000010
!  13*  217332.40   215001.14 80  217344.34 06       BBZ,STSBIT,JWRAM1          -IF TS STACKED              FB000011
!  14*  217333.40   000000.00 31            W CON 1  LV,0,0.0($1)               -GET INT. AD.               FB000012
!  15*  217334.00   000001.22 81  217340.34 02       BB,1.18($1),JWFINI         -IF PP TRIES TO RESTORE EXE FB000013
!  16*  217335.00   217337.41 D0                     SVA,0,WFINI                -SET TOE ADDRESS            FB000014
!  17*  217335.40   000001.00 81  000013.04 A0       TI,2,1.0($1),$IND          -RESTORE IND + MASK REGS.   FB000015
!  18*  217336.40   215245.00 80  000020.10 A0       TI,4,STLR+13.0,$0          -RESTORE USED INDEX REGS    FB000016
!  19*  217337.40   217337.40 00            W FINI   BE,$                       -RETURN TO PP INTERRUPTED ADDRESS FB000017
!  20*  217340.00   215265.01 D0            JWFINI   SVA,$0,STIC                -MUST FAKE EXE              FB000018
!  21*  217340.40 * 000001.00 81  000013.04 A0       TI,2,1.0($1),$IND                                      FB000019
!  22*  217341.40   215245.00 80  000020.10 A0       TI,4,STLR+13.0,$0                                      FB000020
!  23*  217342.40   215125.10 00                     B,SIPT+18.0                - FAKE EXE                  FB000021
!  24*  217343.00   215163.03 01            WRAM     LVI,1,SFPTE                                            FB000022
!  25*  217343.40   217333.50 00                     B,WCON1                                                FB000023
!  26*  217344.00   000000.00 31            JWRAM1   LV,0,0.0($1)                                           FB000024
!  27*  217344.40   215265.01 D0                     SVA,0,STIC                                             FB000025
!  28*  217345.00   000001.00 81  000013.04 A0       TI,2,1.0($1),$IND                                      FB000026
!  29*  217346.00   215245.00 80  000020.10 A0       TI,4,STLR+13.0,$0                                      FB000027
!  30*  217347.00   215107.10 00                     B,SIPT+4.0                 -FAKE TS                    FB000028
!
! Line 30 is a half word, so the counter reaches 217347.40 for
! whatever page follows.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THESE CHECKS DO AND DO NOT ESTABLISH
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! All twenty-five emitting rows are declared, and all six of the
! page's own labels.  Nothing on this page is left unchecked.
!
! THE REAL CHECKS OF THIS PAGE'S OWN COUNTING are the four rows
! whose operand is a label defined HERE:
!   line 13  BBZ,STSBIT,JWRAM1 -> 217344.34, and JWRAM1 is line 26
!   line 15  BB,...,JWFINI     -> 217340.34, and JWFINI is line 20
!   line 16  SVA,0,WFINI       -> 217337.41, and W FINI is line 19
!   line 25  B,WCON1           -> 217333.50, and W CON 1 is line 14
! Each one is a forward or backward reference across the page that
! only resolves if every intervening row's LENGTH is right, and
! they run in both directions.
!
! TAUTOLOGY AUDIT: none.  Every external is defined by a card on
! another page (see EXTERNALS), so no row here is checking a value
! this page itself supplied.
!
! WHAT IS PINNED ONLY TO THE HALF WORD, from this page alone:
!   W JERR (lines 8,10 -- BXL/BZXL), S TIC (lines 20,27 -- SVA),
!   S FPTE (line 24 -- LVI), S IPT (lines 23,30 -- B), W FINI
!   (line 16 -- SVA), W CON 1 (line 25 -- B), S LOWER and S UPPER
!   (lines 7,9 -- KV).  Bit offsets 0-31 all encode identically in
!   those forms, so ".00" is a CONVENTION there and no !CHECK can
!   test it.  Each is nevertheless pinned to the bit by a card
!   elsewhere, cited under EXTERNALS; W FINI and W CON 1 are
!   pinned by their own printed LOCATIONS on lines 19 and 14.
! WHAT IS PINNED TO THE BIT from this page: S SPFIX (line 11) and
!   S TSBIT (line 13), whose operands are full 24-bit bit
!   addresses, and S T LR (lines 12,18, TI's 24-bit A1).
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! TAIL SCOPE, NOT A COLLISION
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! printed p.99 line 11's "SLC,(8)215000." opened the second
! assembly of MCP, and p.98 line 37's "UNTAIL,(2)" had already
! closed p.2's TAIL block, so names here may legitimately repeat
! names that pp.2-98 define at other addresses.  Checked against
! the landed decks: WRAM is already SYN'd at 217343.00 by
! decks/mcp_bootstrap_p133.strap (same value, no conflict);
! W JERR at 216372.00 agrees with decks/mcp_bootstrap_p130.strap's
! definition; S T LR, S UPPER, S LOWER, S TIC, S IPT, S FPTE,
! S SPFIX, S TSBIT and S COM RG all agree with the values the
! landed decks already carry.  WRAMPP, W CON 1, W FINI, JWFINI
! and JWRAM1 are new names that no landed deck carries.  Reported,
! not touched.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! ASSEMBLER LIMITATION HIT: none.
! No printed spelling was rejected by strap_asm except "$C", and
! "$C" is not a system symbol in ANY reading -- see GLYPHS (2),
! where it is read as "$0" on the drum's dropout asymmetry and the
! reading is then confirmed by the printed bits.  Accepted exactly
! as printed: the blank-in-a-label forms "W CON 1" and "W FINI"
! (written closed up, as the deck format requires and as the page's
! own references already print them), "$0" in the index position
! beside the plain "0" form on the same page ("SVA,$0,STIC" line 20
! vs "SVA,0,STIC" line 27), the connective "CM0000(BU,1)", and
! "SLC,$" -- which assembles, and is restated hard here only so the
! deck stands alone; see THE JOIN for what that costs and for the
! two witnesses that pay it back.
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

!SYM   WRAMPP   217326.00
!SYM   WCON1    217333.40
!SYM   WFINI    217337.40
!SYM   JWFINI   217340.00
!SYM   WRAM     217343.00
!SYM   JWRAM1   217344.00
!CHECK 217326.00 | 000021.37 70 | line 6 WRAMPP SR,15,$1 -GET PTOE (printed SLC,$ on line 5 gives this page's arriving counter as 217326.00)
!CHECK 217326.40 | 215230.42 90 | line 7 KV,$1,SLOWER -- S LOWER is 215230.40, the .02 is KV's own operation bits
!CHECK 217327.00 | 216372.32 42 | line 8 BXL,WJERR (same card as line 7)
!CHECK 217327.40 | 215230.02 90 | line 9 KV,$1,SUPPER -- S UPPER is 215230.00
!CHECK 217330.00 | 216372.32 40 | line 10 BZXL,WJERR (same card as line 9)
!CHECK 217330.40 | 215001.13 80 001000.00 F0 | line 11 CM0000(BU,1),SSPFIX -- printed "CMOCOO" and "OC1000.CC FC"; the four connective digits are checked by this row (CM1111 would print 001000.36), and the byte is F0 by the i2 rule
!CHECK 217331.40 | 215234.00 80 000007.02 A0 | line 12 TI,1,STLR+4.0,$LZC -- $AOC would print 000007.42, so .02 checks $LZC
!CHECK 217332.40 | 215001.14 80 217344.34 06 | line 13 BBZ,STSBIT,JWRAM1 -- forward reference to line 26, a real check of this page's counting
!CHECK 217333.40 | 000000.00 31 | line 14 W CON 1 LV,0,0.0($1) -GET INT. AD.
!CHECK 217334.00 | 000001.22 81 217340.34 02 | line 15 BB,1.18($1),JWFINI -- bit 18 written decimal, printed .22 octal; forward reference to line 20
